Meeting summary for 8 October 2025:

  *

    *Updated: Release 2.7*
    OpenVPN 2.7 beta2 was released 25 September.
    It looks like next up will be a beta3, then beta4, after which an
    rc1 or stable release is expected, after the hackathon end of October.
    Tentative date for OpenVPN 2.7 beta3 is 10th of October.
    Tentative date for a beta4 is next week.

  *

    *Updated: wolfSSL license changed from gplv2 to gplv3*
    The release notes of wolfSSL indicate the license changed to GPLv3.
    This basically makes wolfSSL incompatible in regards to licensing
    with OpenVPN.
    There is ongoing communication with wolfSSL regarding this issue,
    they suggested a meeting, we agreed. Currently our position is still
    that if there is no resolution by 15th of October, then OpenVPN
    2.7.0 goes out without wolfSSL support.
    We will reevaluate at next community meeting.

  *

    *Updated: OpenVPN community meetup 2025*
    https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/wiki/CommunityMeetup2025
    When: 25 and 26 october (Saturday and Sunday), with travel days on
    the Friday before and Monday after.
    Where: Naples, Italy.
    Meeting room:https://www.hotelparadisonapoli.it/en/home-page.aspx
    Hotel: Paradiso Napoli Hotel.
    Beer: yes.
    T-shirts: design being made ready. Current status is that Matt came
    up with a good design that meets with approval, and he will deliver
    this over the weekend.

  *

    *Updated: t_server and t_client testing framework*
    mattock reports that he's started publishing his work for t_server
    in this location:
    https://github.com/mattock/openvpn-tests/tree/t_server_template/t_server

  *

    *Updated: forums situation*
    minx from OpenVPN Inc. offered to set up a new forum and help us
    migrate old data to it.
    Unfortunately minx left the company. He did hand over all his work
    though to other people.
    OpenVPN Inc. website team has put this on their roadmap, to work on
    it further. So let's give them a chance.

As always you're welcome to join at #openvpn-meeting on Libera IRC 
network every Wednesday at 14:00 Central European Time.

Kind regards,
Johan Draaisma

